{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.MesonColorTubeUniqueness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.MesonColorTubeUniqueness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Subtype"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.meson_ratio_subsingleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.meson_ratio_subsingleton","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/meson-color-tube-uniqueness.lean#L136-L148","doc":"**Sub-singleton companion.**  Two meson-ratio evaluators\nsharing the same q-character function and the same\nGMOR-via-α_shift identification agree pointwise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.meson_ratio_via_alpha_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.meson_ratio_via_alpha_shift","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/meson-color-tube-uniqueness.lean#L113-L134","doc":"**Meson GMOR uniqueness theorem.**  Given the structural\nfactorisation `m_K² / m_π² = [m]_q · [n]_q` at indices `m, n`,\nand the identification of those indices with `α_shift(T(2, 3))`\nand `α_shift(T(2, 4))` via `MesonForceCarrierPair`, the ratio\nis **uniquely determined** by the substrate q-character function\nat the two pole orders 3 and 4.\n\nPer AGENTS.md §3b-cond: the *form* of the factorisation is\nfixed (3 · 4 in the q-character, via the proved α_shift\nformula); the per-character function `qChar` is the open\nparameter (the `[n]_q` closed form is standard from\nIwahori-Hecke theory, but the substrate-specific evaluation\nrequires the residue / resolvent step shared with PRs #1444\n+ #1445 — the smaller-scope open math). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:meson-color-tube-uniqueness","label":"prop:meson-color-tube-uniqueness","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/meson-color-tube-uniqueness.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instMesonForceCarrierPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instMesonForceCarrierPair","kind":"instance","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/meson-color-tube-uniqueness.lean#L107-L111","doc":"**Default instance** witnessing the meson force-carrier pair —\ndischarges trivially from the proved α_shift specialisations\nabove. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MesonForceCarrierPair.meson_indices_are_alpha_shifts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MesonForceCarrierPair.meson_indices_are_alpha_shifts","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/meson-color-tube-uniqueness.lean#L105-L105","doc":"The two indices `m`, `n` carrying the GMOR factorisation are\n`alphaShift 2 3 = 3` and `alphaShift 2 4 = 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MesonForceCarrierPair.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MesonForceCarrierPair.mk","kind":"ctor","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/meson-color-tube-uniqueness.lean#L102-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MesonForceCarrierPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MesonForceCarrierPair","kind":"class","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/meson-color-tube-uniqueness.lean#L87-L105","doc":"**Meson force-carrier pair.**  The specific torus knots\nunderlying the GMOR factorisation are `T(2, 3)` and `T(2, 4)` —\nthe smallest non-trivial pair on the torus-knot tower, carrying\npole orders 3 and 4 respectively per `prop:alpha-shift-torus-knot`.\n\nPer the α_shift universal derivation chain\n(`docs/audits/2026-05-30-alpha-shift-universal-derivation-chain.md`),\nthis pair is the meson analogue of:\n- the genus-4 Bring pair `{T(2, 9), T(3, 5)}` for α_EM and\n  the p-n averaging weight;\n- the T(2, k) tower for the lepton + electroweak masses.\n\nClosing this class to a Lean-derived instance — i.e., proving\n*why* the smallest non-trivial pair is the meson carrier — is\nthe open mathematical content this file scaffolds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MesonGMORFactorization.factors","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MesonGMORFactorization.factors","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/meson-color-tube-uniqueness.lean#L85-L85","doc":"`m_K² / m_π² (q) = [m]_q · [n]_q` at the substrate value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MesonGMORFactorization.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MesonGMORFactorization.mk","kind":"ctor","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/meson-color-tube-uniqueness.lean#L81-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MesonGMORFactorization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MesonGMORFactorization","kind":"class","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/meson-color-tube-uniqueness.lean#L74-L85","doc":"**Meson GMOR factorisation.**  The substrate-evaluated ratio\n`m_K² / m_π²` factors as a product of two q-character values\nindexed by the α_shift of two torus knots.\n\nThe class records the structural decomposition; the specific\nfactorisation indices (`3` and `4`) and the q-character\nfunction are carried as substrate axioms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QChar","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/meson-color-tube-uniqueness.lean#L63-L72","doc":"A `q`-character function on the substrate: takes the\nsubstrate parameter `q` and the q-integer index `n`, returns\n`[n]_q` in the ground ring `R`.  Pre-Arch: `R` abstract.  Closed\nform: `[n]_q = (q^n - q^{-n}) / (q - q^{-1})`.\n\n§7c: only the ring multiplication of `R` is used below — the GMOR\nfactorisation `m_K²/m_π² = [m]_q·[n]_q` is a product, the closed form\nof `[n]_q` itself is not formalised here — so `[CommRing R]` is the\nweakest typeclass admitting the construction and no field is needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.alphaShift_T_2_4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.alphaShift_T_2_4","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/meson-color-tube-uniqueness.lean#L58-L61","doc":"α_shift(T(2, 4)) = 4·1 = 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.alphaShift_T_2_3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.alphaShift_T_2_3","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/meson-color-tube-uniqueness.lean#L53-L56","doc":"α_shift(T(2, 3)) = 3·1 = 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.alphaShift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.alphaShift","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/meson-color-tube-uniqueness.lean#L47-L51","doc":"The α_shift formula: `alphaShift p k := k * (p - 1)`.  Mirrors\nthe canonical declaration in\n`mass-theory/alpha-shift-torus-knot.lean` for ergonomics here —\nclosing the underlying class instance happens in that file. ","signatureChunk":0}]}